  "verbalization": "Tetracycline appears to be indirectly linked to Yaws through a chain of indications. The evidence suggests that Tetracycline is associated with Ornithosis, which in turn is linked to Sulfisoxazole and finally to Yaws. Similarly, Tetracycline is also associated with Cat-scratch Disease, which is linked to Demeclocycline, which also leads to Yaws. These pathways highlight a potential role for Tetracycline in the treatment of infections that are ultimately linked to Yaws. The overlapping indications suggest that Tetracycline may be used in contexts where other antibiotics, such as Demeclocycline or Sulfisoxazole, are employed, potentially supporting a broader therapeutic use. The integration of these pathways underscores the possibility that Tetracycline could be repurposed for treating Yaws, though further validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
